    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "CALL FOR SCRIPTS DEADLINE"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<div class='et_pb_column et_pb_column_4_4 et_pb_column_0 et_pb_css_mix_blend_mode_passthrough et-last-child'> <div class='et_pb_with_border et_pb_module et_pb_text et_pb_text_0 et_pb_text_align_center et_pb_bg_layout_light'> <div class='et_pb_text_inner'> <div class='et_pb_column et_pb_column_4_4 et_pb_column_0 et_pb_css_mix_blend_mode_passthrough et-last-child'> <div class='et_pb_with_border et_pb_module et_pb_text et_pb_text_0 et_pb_text_align_center et_pb_bg_layout_light'> <div class='et_pb_text_inner'> <div class='et_pb_section et_pb_section_0 et_pb_fullwidth_section et_section_regular'> <div class='et_pb_module et_pb_fullwidth_image et_pb_fullwidth_image_0'></div> </div> <div class='et_pb_section et_pb_section_3 et_pb_with_background et_section_regular'> <div class='et_pb_row et_pb_row_0'> <div class='et_pb_column et_pb_column_4_4 et_pb_column_0 et_pb_css_mix_blend_mode_passthrough et-last-child'> <div class='et_pb_with_border et_pb_module et_pb_text et_pb_text_0 et_pb_text_align_center et_pb_bg_layout_light'> <div class='et_pb_text_inner'> <h1><strong><span class='tm10'>CALL FOR SCRIPTS</span></strong></h1> <p class='tm9 Title'><span class='tm11'>The 17th </span><strong><span class='tm12'>King’s Shorts Festival of Ten Minute Plays </span></strong><span class='tm11'>will be hosted by King’s Theatre in </span><span class='tm11'>Annapolis Royal, Nova Scotia, Canada on </span><strong><span class='tm12'>June 19, 20 &amp; 21, 2026. </span></strong></p> <p><strong>Scripts will be accepted until January 12, 2026.</strong></p> </div> </div> <div class='et_pb_with_border et_pb_module et_pb_text et_pb_text_1 et_pb_text_align_center et_pb_bg_layout_light'> <div class='et_pb_text_inner'> <p><strong>Submission Requirements:</strong></p> <ul> <li>A $20 CAD submission fee must accompany each script submitted.</li> <li><a href='https://purchase.kingstheatre.ca/ChooseSeats/21801'><strong>Payment link is here.</strong></a> (Please ignore references to seating, this is indeed the script submission link.)</li> <li>Scripts should be emailed in PDF format to <a href='mailto:kingsshortsscripts@gmail.com'>kingsshortsscripts@gmail.com</a></li> <li>Deadline January 12, 2026.</li> </ul> <p>For assistance, call the King’s Theatre Box Office at 902-532-7704.</p> </div> </div> <div class='et_pb_with_border et_pb_module et_pb_text et_pb_text_2 et_pb_text_align_center et_pb_bg_layout_light'> <div class='et_pb_text_inner'> <p class='tm7'><span class='tm8'>Entries for the Festival may also be sent by mail. They must be<strong> postmarked no later</strong></span><strong><span class='tm8'> than </span></strong><span class='tm11'><strong>January 12, 2026</strong>, </span><span class='tm8'>with a <strong>non-refundable $20 entry fee per script</strong>. </span><span class='tm11'>Participants are encouraged to use electronic submission, keeping </span><span class='tm8'>in mind that delays with Canada Post may occur: </span><strong><span class='tm14'>King’s Theatre, PO Box 161, </span><span class='tm14'>Annapolis Royal, Nova Scotia, B0S 1A0, Canada.</span></strong></p> </div> </div> <div class='et_pb_with_border et_pb_module et_pb_text et_pb_text_3 et_pb_text_align_center et_pb_bg_layout_light'> <div class='et_pb_text_inner'> <p><strong>Submission Details:</strong></p> <p class='tm7'><span class='tm8'>The Festival is open to all writers and playwrights, </span><span class='tm9'>worldwide</span><span class='tm8'>, even if you have never written a play before. </span><span class='tm8'><strong>To be eligible, scripts must</strong><strong><span class='tm9'> not have been previously produced in any form. </span></strong>Plays may not exceed 10 minutes total stage time. Playwrights may submit a maximum of two plays, using a different pseudonym per script. A non-refundable $20 submission fee must accompany each script.</span></p> <p class='tm7'><span class='tm8'>Requested format is 12-point Courier font (hand-written plays will not be accepted). All pages must be numbered. </span><span class='tm8'>The first page of the play should contain the play’s title and a pseudonym for the playwright. The playwright’s actual name and contact information should be in the submission email, not on the script document. If sending by mail, playwright’s actual name and contact information should be in a sealed envelope, not on the script document</span><span class='tm8'>. This will ensure anonymity during the judging process. </span></p> <p class='tm11'><span class='tm8'>Scripts can be of any genre (comedy, tragedy etc.), and should have a limited number of characters (1-6)<strong>. </strong>Playwrights should avoid wording that might offend a general audience. Because of the nature of the Festival, the sets must be kept simple and be capable of being changed quickly. </span></p> <p class='tm11'><span class='tm8'>The King’s Shorts Reading Committee will choose eight plays, by eight different playwrights, to be staged at King’s Theatre with local directors and actors. Of those eight, one will be chosen by Theatre Nova Scotia as the best written script and receive a prize of $400. A second place best written script, also chosen by Theatre Nova Scotia, will receive a prize of $200. All attending audiences will be asked to vote for the People’s Choice Award, announced at the Sunday matinee on Sunday June 21, 2026.</span></p> <p class='tm11'><u><span class='tm8'>Applicants will be informed by March 13, 2026 if their play is to be included in the Festival. </span></u><span class='tm8'>Scripts will not be returned. </span></p> <p class='tm11'><span class='tm9'>For further information, contact King’s Shorts Committee Volunteer Verilea Ellis at 902-245-2309</span></p> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> "
      }
    ],
