    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "CALL FOR SCRIPTS DEADLINE"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n                \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCALL FOR SCRIPTS\nThe 17th King’s Shorts Festival of Ten Minute Plays will be hosted by King’s Theatre in Annapolis Royal, Nova Scotia, Canada on June 19, 20 & 21, 2026. \nScripts will be accepted until January 12, 2026.\n\n\n\n\nSubmission Requirements:\n\nA $20 CAD submission fee must accompany each script submitted.\nPayment link is here. (Please ignore references to seating, this is indeed the script submission link.)\nScripts should be emailed in PDF format to kingsshortsscripts@gmail.com\nDeadline January 12, 2026.\n\nFor assistance, call the King’s Theatre Box Office at 902-532-7704.\n\n\n\n\nEntries for the Festival may also be sent by mail. They must be postmarked no later than January 12, 2026, with a non-refundable $20 entry fee per script. Participants are encouraged to use electronic submission, keeping in mind that delays with Canada Post may occur: King’s Theatre, PO Box 161, Annapolis Royal, Nova Scotia, B0S 1A0, Canada.\n\n\n\n\nSubmission Details:\nThe Festival is open to all writers and playwrights, worldwide, even if you have never written a play before. To be eligible, scripts must not have been previously produced in any form. Plays may not exceed 10 minutes total stage time. Playwrights may submit a maximum of two plays, using a different pseudonym per script. A non-refundable $20 submission fee must accompany each script.\nRequested format is 12-point Courier font (hand-written plays will not be accepted). All pages must be numbered. The first page of the play should contain the play’s title and a pseudonym for the playwright. The playwright’s actual name and contact information should be in the submission email, not on the script document. If sending by mail, playwright’s actual name and contact information should be in a sealed envelope, not on the script document. This will ensure anonymity during the judging process. \nScripts can be of any genre (comedy, tragedy etc.), and should have a limited number of characters (1-6). Playwrights should avoid wording that might offend a general audience. Because of the nature of the Festival, the sets must be kept simple and be capable of being changed quickly. \nThe King’s Shorts Reading Committee will choose eight plays, by eight different playwrights, to be staged at King’s Theatre with local directors and actors. Of those eight, one will be chosen by Theatre Nova Scotia as the best written script and receive a prize of $400. A second place best written script, also chosen by Theatre Nova Scotia, will receive a prize of $200. All attending audiences will be asked to vote for the People’s Choice Award, announced at the Sunday matinee on Sunday June 21, 2026.\nApplicants will be informed by March 13, 2026 if their play is to be included in the Festival. Scripts will not be returned. \nFor further information, contact King’s Shorts Committee Volunteer Verilea Ellis at 902-245-2309\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n            "
      }
    ],
