    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "THE HETEROSEXUALS"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<div><span style='color: #000000;'>★★★★★ “Comic genius!” The Irish Times<br /> ★★★★★ “Priceless, playful perfection!” The Reviews Hub</span></div> <div><span style='color: #000000;'> </span></div> <p><span class='x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs xlh3980 xvmahel x1n0sxbx x1lliihq x1s928wv xhkezso x1gmr53x x1cpjm7i x1fgarty x1943h6x xudqn12 x3x7a5m x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1l8bm xzsf02u x1yc453h' dir='auto'><strong>A comedic deep dive into the mysterious world of heterosexuality, from charismatic Toronto actor, writer and comedian Johnnie McNamara Walker.</strong> </span></p> <p><span class='x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs xlh3980 xvmahel x1n0sxbx x1lliihq x1s928wv xhkezso x1gmr53x x1cpjm7i x1fgarty x1943h6x xudqn12 x3x7a5m x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1l8bm xzsf02u x1yc453h' dir='auto'>Heterosexuals…THEY WALK AMONG US! But where did they come from? And what do they think they’re wearing? Find out in this explosive solo show based on undercover research gathered while posing as one of their own! Combining elements of storytelling, satire, comedy, and deep personal humiliation, The Heterosexuals is here to spill the Tea on what The Queers really think about The Straights.</span></p> <div><span style='color: #000000;'>The latest solo show from tour-de-force writer/performer Johnnie McNamara Walker has wowed audiences and sold out houses across Canada as well as touring internationally to Ireland and the US, including an Off-Broadway run at The SoHo Playhouse in NYC.</span></div> <ul> <li><strong>Winner: English Comedy Award</strong> <em>(Montreal Fringe)</em></li> <li><strong>Winner: Outstanding Theatre Award </strong><em>(fringereview.co.uk)</em></li> <li><strong>Winner: Audience Favourite Award</strong> <em>(Lavender Fest)</em></li> <li><strong>Finalist: Fringe Encore Series</strong> <em>(Soho playhouse)</em></li> </ul> <p><strong><span style='color: #000000;'>Johnnie McNamara Walker</span></strong> is a writer and performer from Toronto who has been producing work for the stage for twenty years. He continues to tour his solo shows The Heterosexuals and Iggy Beamish Destroys Traditional Marriage both across Canada and internationally, including a recent Off-Broadway debut at The SoHo Playhouse in New York City. His first solo show, Redheaded Stepchild, toured Canada coast-to-coast and was published by Playwrights Canada Press. His play Shove It Down My Throatpremiered at Buddies in Bad Times Theatre in Toronto as part of their 40th Anniversary Season in 2019. Johnnie is also a founding member of BoylesqueTO and has written and hosted dozens of shows for the troupe, which have been performed across North America and been honoured at the Burlesque Hall of Fame in Las Vegas.</p> <p><em><strong>Recommended for audiences 13+. Light cursing and sexual content.</strong></em></p> <p><strong>TICKETS:</strong><strong>  </strong></p> <ul> <li style='list-style-type: none;'> <ul> <li><strong>Adults $45 </strong></li> <li><strong>Supported $25</strong></li> <li><strong>Youth $15</strong></li> <li>HST additional</li> </ul> </li> <li style='list-style-type: none;'> <ul> <li><em>Doors open 45 minutes before showtime. Please arrive early.</em></li> </ul> </li> <li class='style__notes___25v7J'> <div class='main-title'> <div class='TitleBlock__TitleMetaDataContainer-sc-1nlhx7j-2 hWHMKr'> <ul> <li style='list-style-type: none;'> <ul> <li><em>King’s Theatre is committed to accessibility. If price is a barrier to attending, please request a ‘Bursary Ticket’ at the Box Office.</em></li> <li><em>Tickets are not refundable for cash, but can be exchanged for credit with a <span style='text-decoration: underline;'>minimum of 48 hours notice</span>. Credits are valid for 12 months.</em></li> <li><em>All persons require a ticket; we do not allow babes in arms. Children under 12 must be accompanied by a guardian.</em></li> <li><em>Outside food and beverages may not be brought into the theatre.</em></li> <li><em>For more information about Theatre policies, click <a href='https://www.kingstheatre.ca/about/ticket-info/'>here.</a></em></li> </ul> </li> </ul> </div> </div> </li> <li></li> <li class='wpview wpview-wrap' contenteditable='false' data-wpview-text='https%3A%2F%2Fyoutu.be%2FdoQmVCJCiAk' data-wpview-type='embedURL'><iframe title='The Heterosexuals by Johnnie McNamara Walker - trailer' src='https://www.youtube.com/embed/doQmVCJCiAk?feature=oembed' width='709' height='399' allowfullscreen='allowfullscreen'></iframe></li> </ul> "
      }
    ],
