    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "HAMLET"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n                \n\n\n‘The play’s the thing’. Something is rotten in the state of Denmark. Are you watching closely? Trapped between duty and doubt, surrounded by power and privilege, young Prince Hamlet dares to ask the ultimate question – you know the one.\nOlivier Award-winner Hiran Abeysekera (The Father and the Assassin, Life of Pi) is Hamlet in this fearless, contemporary take on Shakespeare’s famous tragedy. National Theatre Deputy Artistic Director, Robert Hastie (Standing at the Sky’s Edge, Operation Mincemeat) directs this sharp, stylish and darkly funny reimagining.\n\n\n\n★★★★★ ‘Exactly the kind of Hamlet you would hope to see at The National Theatre’ Broadway World \n★★★★ ‘Sharp, stylish and darkly funny’ All That Dazzles \n★★★★ Abeysekera’s Hamlet is charming, cheeky and cunning’ The Upcoming\n\n\n\n\n\n\nEstimated Run Time 2 hours 50 minutes including interval\nTICKETS\n\nAdult: $16.95\nYouth: $7.95\nHST additional\n\n\n\n\nDoors open 45 minutes before showtime. Please arrive early.\nKing’s Theatre is committed to accessibility. If price is a barrier to attending, please request a ‘Bursary Ticket’ at the Box Office.\nTickets are not refundable for cash, but can be exchanged for credit with a minimum of 48 hours notice. Credits are valid for 12 months.\nAll persons require a ticket; we do not allow babes in arms. Children under 12 must be accompanied by a guardian.\nOutside food and beverages may not be brought into the theatre.\nFor more information about Theatre policies, click here.\n\n\n\n\n            "
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/eventStatus": [
      {
        "@id": "http://schema.org/EventScheduled"
      }
    ]
  },
