    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "THERESA MALENFANT & KIM DOOLITTLE"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n                Get ready for a big night of WOMEN SINGING THE BLUES with Theresa Malenfant & Scott Medford, and Kim Doolittle & John Ebata\nTheresa Malenfant & Scott Medford \nECMA winner Theresa Malenfant and renowned guitarist Scott Medford have become one of the most popular blues duo acts in the Atlantic Provinces. They have been performing together in a band for years, but decided to work as a duo only 6 years ago. In that short time they managed to win second place in an International Blues Challenge (IBC) held in Memphis Tennessee.\nKim Doolittle & John Ebata\nKim Dootlittle is an Original Artist born in rural Nova Scotia and did her first paid gig as a child. She was a fixture in the Toronto Music Scene for many years playing Festivals and Events, competed in the International Blues Challenge in 2016 and 2020 & has shared the stage with Jeff Healey, Downchild Blues Band, Suzie Vinnick, Ken Whiteley and many more. She’s travelled the Globe with her Guitar in hand and feels like a Road Scholar —sharing her Muse through song and will be dropping her 10th album in 2026.\nJohn Ebata is respected in all the extended categories of musician, song writer, producer, musical director, arranger and recording engineer. Equally versatile in all musical styles from jazz to world folk songs to rock and R&B, he has become the first choice accompanist of many great singer songwriters and  acclaimed to be of the very top Canadian piano-keyboardists and continues to work with artists from all parts of the world.\n\nTICKETS:  \n\nAdults: $35\nYouth: $10\nHST additional\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDoors open 45 minutes before showtime. Please arrive early.\nKing’s Theatre is committed to accessibility. If price is a barrier to attending, please request a ‘Bursary Ticket’ at the Box Office.\nTickets are not refundable for cash, but can be exchanged for credit with a minimum of 48 hours notice. Credits are valid for 12 months.\nAll persons require a ticket; we do not allow babes in arms. Children under 12 must be accompanied by a guardian.\nOutside food and beverages may not be brought into the theatre.\nFor more information about Theatre policies, click here.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n            "
      }
    ],
