  {
    "@id": "https://www.kingstheatre.ca/new-events/annapolis-guitar-quartet/event_242270_0",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Event"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.kingstheatre.ca/new-events/annapolis-guitar-quartet/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.kingstheatre.ca/kingweb/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Annapolis_GQ4-1.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.kingstheatre.ca/new-events/annapolis-guitar-quartet/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "ANNAPOLIS GUITAR QUARTET"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<p><strong>The Amadeus Guitar Duo (Dale Kavanagh &amp; Thomas Kirchhoff) and the Duo Cormier-Martin (Eugene Cormier &amp; Matthew Martin) have come together to create the</strong> <strong>ANNAPOLIS GUITAR QUARTET</strong>.</p> <p>Experience the incredible energy of four virtuoso classical guitars playing works by Boccherini, Jenkins, Spanish and tango composers, and much more.</p> <p>The Amadeus Guitar Duo and the Duo Cormier-Martin have known each other for many years after meeting at guitar and music festivals around the world. The love of programs with great diversity motivated the four musicians to create an evening with works for one, two and four guitars. Works by Handel, Bach and other baroque composers, as well as classical and romantic music, but also modern music dedicated to the duos by Dale Kavanagh and Carlo Domenico make up the Guitar Gala Night &#8211; a concert evening with virtuoso, lyrical and expressive music full of temperament.</p> <p>The Amadeus Guitar Duo with Canadian guitarist Dale Kavanagh and Thomas Kirchhoff of Germany have been playing together since 1992. They performed more than 1.800 concerts in over 80 countries around the world and have produced 20 CDs (NAXOS Int.) – they are regarded as one of the best classical guitar duos of our time. The Canadian Cormier-Martin Duo have been playing together since 2010. Cormier and Martin are both teaching at Acadia University in Wolfville, NS.</p> <div id='i8e4vmc5' class='BaOVQ8 tz5f0K i8e4vmc5 wixui-rich-text' data-testid='richTextElement'> <p><strong>TICKETS:</strong><strong>  </strong></p> <ul> <li><strong>Adults: $35</strong></li> <li><strong>Youth: $10</strong></li> <li>HST additional</li> </ul> </div> <p><span style='text-decoration: underline;'><strong>Program</strong></span></p> <ul> <li><strong>Luigi Boccherini</strong> (1743-1805)  Quintet No 4 in D-major (quartet) &#8211; Fandango</li> <li><strong>Carlo Domeniconi </strong> (b. 1947)  Oyun (quartet) Molto energico &#8211; Lento – Con Fuoco</li> <li><strong>Jaime M. Zenamon</strong> (b. 1953) Casablanca (duo) A place, a story and a kiss</li> <li><strong>Gaspar Sanz (</strong>1640-1710) Espagnoleta y Canarios (duo)</li> <li><strong>Dale Kavanagh</strong> (b. 1958) Impressions (2015) (solo)</li> <li>&#8212;&#8212; I N T E R M I S S I O N &#8212;&#8212;</li> <li><strong>Maximo Diego</strong> (b. 1957) Pujol Tango, Milonga y Final (duo)</li> <li><strong>F. Moreno Torroba</strong> (1891-1982) Estampas (quartet)  Bailando un Fandango Charro/ La Boda &#8211; Camino del Molino/ Juegos Infantiles</li> <li><strong>Dale Kavanagh</strong> (b. 1958) Loon Lake, op. 18 (quartet) for the Vancouver Guitar Society</li> <li><strong>Karl Jenkins</strong> (b. 1944) Palladio (quartet)</li> </ul> <hr /> <p><iframe title='ANNAPOLIS GUITAR QUARTET- LIVE MUSIC AT KING&#039;S!' width='1080' height='608' src='https://www.youtube.com/embed/JyPEVRCtf2U?feature=oembed'  allow='accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share' referrerpolicy='strict-origin-when-cross-origin' allowfullscreen></iframe></p> <ul> <li><em>Doors open 45 minutes before showtime. Please arrive early.</em></li> <li><em>King’s Theatre is committed to accessibility. If price is a barrier to attending, please request a ‘Bursary Ticket’ at the Box Office.</em></li> <li><em>Tickets are not refundable for cash, but can be exchanged for credit with a minimum of 48 hours notice. Credits are valid for 12 months.</em></li> <li><em>All persons require a ticket; we do not allow babes in arms. Children under 12 must be accompanied by a guardian.</em></li> <li><em>Outside food and beverages may not be brought into the theatre.</em></li> <li><em>For more information about Theatre policies, click <a href='https://www.kingstheatre.ca/about/ticket-info/'>here.</a></em></li> </ul> <p>&nbsp;</p> <div style='position: relative; padding-top: max(60%,326px); height: 0; width: 100%;'><iframe style='position: absolute; border: none; width: 100%; height: 100%; left: 0; right: 0; top: 0; bottom: 0;' title='Annapolis Guitar Quartet Program - 03-22-26' src='https://e.issuu.com/embed.html?d=annapolis_guitar_quartet_program_-_03-22-26&amp;u=kingstheatreannapolisroyal' sandbox='allow-top-navigation allow-top-navigation-by-user-activation allow-downloads allow-scripts allow-same-origin allow-popups allow-modals allow-popups-to-escape-sandbox allow-forms' allowfullscreen='allowfullscreen'></iframe></div> "
      }
    ],
