  {
    "@id": "https://kingstheatre.ca/events/event_242334_0",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Event"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.kingstheatre.ca/new-events/the-skeleton-dance/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.kingstheatre.ca/kingweb/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Screenshot-2025-11-21-at-12.56.37-PM.png"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://kingstheatre.ca/events/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "THE SKELETON DANCE"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<div id='item-62e01b9b77c6355ecaa95034' class='sqs-layout sqs-grid-12 columns-12' data-layout-label='Post Body' data-type='item' data-updated-on='1658854556125'> <div id='yui_3_17_2_1_1763739098427_281' class='row sqs-row'> <div id='yui_3_17_2_1_1763739098427_280' class='col sqs-col-12 span-12'> <div id='block-0c7569a975872279d4b7' class='sqs-block html-block sqs-block-html' data-block-type='2' data-border-radii='{&quot;topLeft&quot;:{&quot;unit&quot;:&quot;px&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:0.0},&quot;topRight&quot;:{&quot;unit&quot;:&quot;px&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:0.0},&quot;bottomLeft&quot;:{&quot;unit&quot;:&quot;px&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:0.0},&quot;bottomRight&quot;:{&quot;unit&quot;:&quot;px&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:0.0}}' data-sqsp-block='text'> <div class='sqs-block-content'> <div class='sqs-html-content' data-sqsp-text-block-content=''> <p class=''>The Skeleton Dance is a highly physical, energetic, and light-hearted play with elements of clown and puppetry. Created and performed by Emma James (they/she) and Ella MacDonald (she/her), it is an all ages about death.</p> <p class=''>In The Skeleton Dance, two young children process the news that their Great Uncle Trout has suddenly passed away. They consider the implications of this in an entertaining, irreverent way, where the audience is privy to their many whimsical theories about death.</p> <p class=''>Emma &amp; Ella believe that everyone has grieved something, be it a loved one, important events, or normalcy. The goal of The Skeleton Dance is to provoke thought about the ways in which we respond to hardship and comfort one another.</p> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <p><strong>TICKETS: </strong></p> <ul> <li><strong>$25 Adults</strong></li> <li><strong>$15 Youth/Supported</strong></li> </ul> <div class='style__notes___25v7J'> <div class='main-title'> <div class='TitleBlock__TitleMetaDataContainer-sc-1nlhx7j-2 hWHMKr'> <div class='style__notes___25v7J'> <div class='main-title'> <div class='TitleBlock__TitleMetaDataContainer-sc-1nlhx7j-2 hWHMKr'> <p><em>HST additional</em></p> <ul> <li style='list-style-type: none;'> <ul> <li><em>Doors open 45 minutes before showtime. Please arrive early.</em></li> <li><em>King’s Theatre is committed to accessibility. If price is a barrier to attending, please request a ‘Bursary Ticket’ at the Box Office.</em></li> <li><em>Tickets are not refundable for cash, but can be exchanged for credit with a minimum of 48 hours notice. Credits are valid for 12 months.</em></li> <li><em>All persons require a ticket; we do not allow babes in arms. Children under 12 must be accompanied by a guardian.</em></li> <li><em>Outside food and beverages may not be brought into the theatre.</em></li> <li><em>For more information about Theatre policies, click <a href='https://www.kingstheatre.ca/about/ticket-info/'>here.</a></em></li> </ul> </li> </ul> </div> </div> </div> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> </div> </div> </div> <div> <div class='style__notes___25v7J'> <div class='main-title'> <div class='TitleBlock__TitleMetaDataContainer-sc-1nlhx7j-2 hWHMKr'></div> </div> </div> </div> "
      }
    ],
