  {
    "@id": "https://kingstheatre.ca/events/event_242318_0",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Event"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.kingstheatre.ca/new-events/gina-burgess/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.kingstheatre.ca/kingweb/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/GinaB-StudioSession-19.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://kingstheatre.ca/events/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "GINA BURGESS"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<div class='elementor-element elementor-element-3e654ce5 elementor-widget elementor-widget-theme-post-content' data-id='3e654ce5' data-element_type='widget' data-widget_type='theme-post-content.default'> <div class='elementor-widget-container'> <p><strong>Gina Burgess</strong> is a genre-bending violinist and composer from Kjipuktuk / Halifax. She is well known for her virtuosic work with the hot swing outfit <strong>Gypsophilia</strong> (NS), and the Juno nominated folk-rock band <strong>The Jerry Cans</strong> (Iqaluit).</p> <p>She&#8217;ll be performing with <strong>Cynthia Pitsiulak</strong> (Contemporary Inuit throat singing), <strong>Greg Woolner</strong> (Drum kit), <strong>Jordan Stephens </strong>(Double bass), and  <strong>Ross Burns </strong>(Brazilian percussion).</p> <p>Gina&#8217;s 2024 debut solo release “ISNOW” was met with wide acclaim, and won an East Coast Music Award for Fusion Recording of The Year.Gina’s performances feature an all-star 5-piece band, combining her violin with contemporary Inuit throat singing, drum kit, double bass, and Brazilian percussion in a wildly unique cross-cultural fusion. Her original music draws inspiration from minimalism, folk and improvised music and her shows are a heartfelt, hypnotizing and engaging experience.</p> <p>“The inspired and talented Canadian artist Gina Burgess presents us with an instrumental piece of unimaginable magnitude, where rhythmic nuances unfold in a perfect musical spectrum, showcasing the refined technique and inspiration of an impressive musician.” &#8212; Roadie Music</p> <p>“…the song, which blends psychedelic elements with Celtic and Inuit roots, takes us into a magical and mischievous fairy world shimmering with fireflies and secrets.” &#8212; Canadian Beats Magazine</p> <p>“Without fear of being wrong, we can say that, since Jean-Luc Ponty, we haven&#8217;t heard such a beautiful original composition, focused on the waves of the violin, as the one we witness in SOS.”</p> <p><strong>TICKETS:</strong></p> <ul> <li><strong>Adults: $30</strong></li> <li><strong>Youth: $10</strong></li> <li>HST additional</li> </ul> <div class='TitleBlock__TitleMetaDataContainer-sc-1nlhx7j-2 hWHMKr'> <ul> <li style='list-style-type: none;'> <ul> <li><em>Doors open 45 minutes before showtime. Please arrive early.</em></li> <li><em>King’s Theatre is committed to accessibility. If price is a barrier to attending, please request a ‘Bursary Ticket’ at the Box Office.</em></li> <li><em>Tickets are not refundable for cash, but can be exchanged for credit with a minimum of 48 hours notice. Credits are valid for 12 months.</em></li> <li><em>All persons require a ticket; we do not allow babes in arms. Children under 12 must be accompanied by a guardian.</em></li> <li><em>Outside food and beverages may not be brought into the theatre.</em></li> <li><em>For more information about Theatre policies, click <a href='https://www.kingstheatre.ca/about/ticket-info/'>here.</a></em></li> </ul> </li> </ul> </div> <p>&nbsp;</p> </div> </div> <p><iframe title='Ravens on the Roof (Official Video)' width='1080' height='608' src='https://www.youtube.com/embed/kImvfE71u_Y?feature=oembed'  allow='accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share' referrerpolicy='strict-origin-when-cross-origin' allowfullscreen></iframe></p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> "
      }
    ],
