    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "MACBETH"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<p><strong>Jeremy Watkin&#8217;s Presents:</strong></p> <h6><strong>MACBETH by William Shakespeare</strong></h6> <p><strong>Adapted, Directed and Produced by Jeremy Watkins</strong></p> <p><em>A King’s desire to kill innocence ignites a tale of manipulation, ambition, and consequence across distant worlds. An honourable warrior, a coercive wife, and the unweaving of their minds—and Scotia itself—when the choice of regicide is made.</em></p> <p><strong>CAST</strong></p> <ul> <li dir='auto'><strong>David Priddle:</strong> King Duncan / The Doctor</li> <li dir='auto'><strong>William Upton:</strong> Malcolm</li> <li dir='auto'><strong>Ryder Miller:</strong> Donalbain / Young Siward</li> <li dir='auto'><strong>Mitchell Muise:</strong> Siward / Porter</li> <li dir='auto'><strong>Allison Amirault:</strong> Macbeth</li> <li dir='auto'><strong>Ingrid d&#8217;Eon:</strong> Lady Macbeth</li> <li dir='auto'><strong>Mia Chute</strong>: Seyton</li> <li dir='auto'><strong>Phillip Cottreau:</strong> Banquo</li> <li dir='auto'><strong>Lee House:</strong> Fleance / Ross</li> <li dir='auto'><strong>Danny Jackson:</strong> Macduff</li> <li dir='auto'><strong>Tracey Jackson:</strong> Lady Macduff / Gentlewoman</li> <li dir='auto'><strong>Connor Huskins:</strong> Lennox / Sergant</li> <li dir='auto'>The Three Sisters / Three Murderers</li> <li dir='auto'><strong>Krista Perry:</strong> Life Sister / Murderer 1</li> <li dir='auto'><strong>Lise Murphy:</strong> Death Sister / Murderer 2</li> <li dir='auto'><strong>Amy Amirault:</strong> Transition Sister / Murderer 3</li> <li dir='auto'><strong>Ellie LeBlanc:</strong> Hecate / Hector</li> </ul> <p><strong>TICKETS:</strong></p> <ul> <li><strong>Adults: $22</strong></li> <li><strong>Youth: $10 (Under 18)</strong></li> </ul> <div class='TitleBlock__TitleMetaDataContainer-sc-1nlhx7j-2 hWHMKr'> <ul> <li style='list-style-type: none;'> <ul> <li><em>Doors open 45 minutes before showtime.</em></li> <li><em>King’s Theatre is committed to accessibility. If price is a barrier to attending, please request a ‘Bursary Ticket’ at the Box Office.</em></li> <li><em>Tickets are not refundable for cash, but can be exchanged for credit with a minimum of 48 hours notice. Credits are valid for 12 months.</em></li> <li><em>All persons require a ticket; we do not allow babes in arms. Children under 12 must be accompanied by a guardian.</em></li> <li><em>Outside food and beverages may not be brought into the theatre.</em></li> <li><em>For more information about Theatre policies, click <a href='https://www.kingstheatre.ca/about/ticket-info/'>here.</a></em></li> </ul> </li> </ul> </div> "
      }
    ],
