  {
    "@id": "https://kingstheatre.ca/events/event_242811_0",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Event"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.kingstheatre.ca/new-events/waterwalker-film-festival/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.kingstheatre.ca/kingweb/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/pff-2025-thumbnail-wild-sea.webp"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://kingstheatre.ca/events/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "WATERWALKER FILM FESTIVAL"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<div id='movie-details-expander'> <div class='score-wrap'> <div class='description-wrap'> <div data-adsmediascorecardmanager='description'> <div class='drawer'> <div class='score-wrap'> <p><strong>We are excited to bring you some of the best films of the 2025 WATERWALKER Film Festival!</strong></p> <p><em><strong>Proudly sponsored by Canoe Annapolis County</strong></em></p> <p>Paddle Canada’s Waterwalker Film Festival is a tribute to the late Bill Mason, a great conservationist, canoeist, and filmmaker who cared passionately about his work and the wilderness. He wanted to share its beauty and promote its protection. As he once said, “Film is for me a means of expressing my feelings about the things I enjoy, things I am concerned about, mostly the natural world”.</p> <p>The Waterwalker Film Festival came together following Mason’s death to help continue his vision. We know you&#8217;ll enjoy the incredible selection of films from around the world. We also hope you will be encouraged and motivated to get involved with the protection and conservation of our wilderness and waterways.</p> <p class='p1'><strong>Come and experience the WATERWALKER Film Festival!</strong></p> <p><img class='alignnone wp-image-242814' src='https://www.kingstheatre.ca/kingweb/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Screenshot-2026-03-26-at-1.50.29-PM-300x114.png' alt='' width='234' height='89' /></p> <div class='description-wrap'> <div data-adsmediascorecardmanager='description'> <p><strong>TICKETS:</strong><br /> <strong>$11.95 Adult</strong><br /> <strong>$7.95 Youth (under 18)</strong><br /> (HST additional)</p> <ul class='p-rich_text_list p-rich_text_list__ordered p-rich_text_list--nested' data-stringify-type='ordered-list' data-list-tree='true' data-indent='0' data-border='0'> <li data-stringify-indent='0' data-stringify-border='0'><em>Doors open 45 minutes before showtime.</em></li> <li data-stringify-indent='0' data-stringify-border='0'><em>King’s Theatre is committed to accessibility. If price is a barrier to attending, please request a ‘Bursary Ticket’ at the Box Office.</em></li> <li data-stringify-indent='0' data-stringify-border='0'><em>Tickets are not refundable for cash, but can be exchanged for credit with a minimum of 48 hours notice. Credits are valid for 12 months.</em></li> <li data-stringify-indent='0' data-stringify-border='0'><em>All persons require a ticket; we do not allow babes in arms. Children under 12 must be accompanied by a guardian.</em></li> <li data-stringify-indent='0' data-stringify-border='0'><em>Outside food and beverages may not be brought into the theatre.</em></li> <li data-stringify-indent='0' data-stringify-border='0'><em>For more information about Theatre policies, click <a href='https://www.kingstheatre.ca/about/ticket-info/'>here.</a></em></li> </ul> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> "
      }
    ],
