    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "KING&#039;S SHORTS"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<p class='tm9 Title'><span class='tm11'>The 17th </span><strong><span class='tm12'>King’s Shorts Festival of Ten Minute Plays </span></strong><span class='tm11'>will be hosted by King’s Theatre in </span><span class='tm11'>Annapolis Royal, Nova Scotia on </span><strong><span class='tm12'>June 19, 20 &amp; 21, 2026.</span></strong></p> <p class='tm9 Title'>The Reading Committee reviewed over 140 submissions and is pleased to announce that the following scripts have been selected to be performed at King&#8217;s Shorts 2026:</p> <div class='x14z9mp xat24cr x1lziwak x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a'> <ul> <li dir='auto'>&#8216;A Fool&#8217;s Folly’ by Carl Williams, Houston, Texas</li> <li dir='auto'>‘Dad&#8217;s Last Cigarette’ by Nancy Anderson, Annapolis Royal, Nova Scotia</li> <li dir='auto'>‘Prime Real Estate’ by Dan Borengasser, Springdale, Arkansas</li> <li dir='auto'>‘Singles and Doubles’ by Donald Loftus, New York, New York</li> <li dir='auto'>‘The Cold Read’ by Harsh Hundal, Kelowna, British Columbia</li> <li dir='auto'>To Feel the Effects’ by Brandon Hicks, St. Stephen, New Brunswick</li> <li dir='auto'>‘Wheel’ by Tim Lehnert, Cranston, Rhode Island</li> </ul> </div> <div class='x14z9mp xat24cr x1lziwak x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a'> <div dir='auto'></div> <div dir='auto'>Congratulations all Playwrights!</div> </div> <div class='x14z9mp xat24cr x1lziwak x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a'> <div dir='auto'></div> </div> <p><strong>TICKETS:</strong></p> <ul> <li><strong>Adults: $22</strong></li> <li><strong>Youth: $10 (Under 18)</strong></li> </ul> <div class='TitleBlock__TitleMetaDataContainer-sc-1nlhx7j-2 hWHMKr'> <ul> <li style='list-style-type: none;'> <ul> <li><em>Doors open 45 minutes before showtime. Please arrive early.</em></li> <li><em>King’s Theatre is committed to accessibility. If price is a barrier to attending, please request a ‘Bursary Ticket’ at the Box Office.</em></li> <li><em>Tickets are not refundable for cash, but can be exchanged for credit with a minimum of 48 hours notice. Credits are valid for 12 months.</em></li> <li><em>All persons require a ticket; we do not allow babes in arms. Children under 12 must be accompanied by a guardian.</em></li> <li><em>Outside food and beverages may not be brought into the theatre.</em></li> <li><em>For more information about Theatre policies, click <a href='https://www.kingstheatre.ca/about/ticket-info/'>here.</a></em></li> </ul> </li> </ul> </div> "
      }
    ],
