  {
    "@id": "https://kingstheatre.ca/events/event_242392_0",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Event"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.kingstheatre.ca/new-events/john-prine-tribute/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.kingstheatre.ca/kingweb/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/MAX_Prine-1920-1005-noartists_page-0001-scaled.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://kingstheatre.ca/events/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "JOHN PRINE TRIBUTE"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<p><strong>In Spite of Ourselves: The Quintessential John Prine Tribute</strong></p> <p>A memorable evening of John Prine’s finest songs &amp; stories, performed by eight seasoned veteran songwriter/musicians’ and friends’, who are lifelong fans of John Prine. A show that includes a multimedia layer of captivating still pics.</p> <p>John Prine is widely cited as one of the most influential songwriters of his generation and was known for humorous &amp; insightful lyrics about love, life, and current events, as well as his serious songs with social commentary and songs that recollect melancholy tales from his life.</p> <p>According to Bob Dylan &#8220;Prine&#8217;s stuff is pure, Proustian, existentialism, Midwestern mind trips to the nth degree, and he writes beautiful songs.” Join us as we celebrate &amp; elaborate on the beautiful songs of one of the finest songwriters of our generation.</p> <p><strong>Join Blair Packham</strong> (The Jitters), <strong>Bill Craig</strong> (The Irish Rovers), <strong>Kirsten Jones</strong> and two-time Juno award nominee <strong>Johnny Max</strong>, as they perform a repertoire of Prine that resonates with audiences far and wide.</p> <p class='tm7'><strong><span class='tm9'>TICKETS</span></strong></p> <ul class='tm11'> <li class='tm12'><strong><span class='tm9'> Adults $40.00</span></strong></li> <li class='tm13'><strong><span class='tm9'>Youth: $15.00</span></strong></li> </ul> <p><em><span class='tm14'>HST additional</span></em></p> <ul> <li><em>Doors open 45 minutes before showtime.</em></li> <li><em>King’s Theatre is committed to accessibility. If price is a barrier to attending, please request a ‘Bursary Ticket’ at the Box Office.</em></li> <li><em>Tickets are not refundable for cash, but can be exchanged for credit with a minimum of 48 hours notice. Credits are valid for 12 months.</em></li> <li><em>All persons require a ticket; we do not allow babes in arms. Children under 12 must be accompanied by a guardian.</em></li> <li><em>Outside food and beverages may not be brought into the theatre.</em></li> <li><em>For more information about Theatre policies, click <a href='https://www.kingstheatre.ca/about/ticket-info/'>here.</a></em></li> </ul> <p class='tm7'> "
      }
    ],
