  {
    "@id": "https://kingstheatre.ca/events/event_242547_0",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Event"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.kingstheatre.ca/new-events/lennie-gallant-2/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.kingstheatre.ca/kingweb/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/lenniegallant.webp"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://kingstheatre.ca/events/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "LENNIE GALLANT"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<div dir='ltr'> <div dir='ltr'> <div dir='ltr'> <div dir='ltr'> <p><strong>Lennie Gallant and band return to King&#8217;s Theatre with The Innkeeper’s Christmas!</strong></p> <p>The highly popular multimedia show will feature songs from Lennie&#8217;s Christmas record, as well as favourites from his extensive catalogue of original songs. It’s an evening full of original Christmas songs, (and some traditional ones), a lot of laughs, great tales, and occasional surprises that will definitely put you in a Yuletide state of mind. This show tends to sell out, so book your tickets early.</p> <p>Lennie released his first Christmas album in 2021 to much praise and critical acclaim. Canadian music reviewer Bob Mersereau said, “I always make a point of listening to many new Christmas albums each year, and this is one of the best I’ve heard in years, and certainly one of the premiere sets of new tunes in a long time!” The title song “Christmas Day On Planet Earth” and its accompanying video is even fast becoming a holiday standard.</p> <p>Lennie&#8217;s band includes his partner, Acadian star Patricia Richard, plus PEI musical phenom Keelin Wedge, piano marvel Julien Robichaud, and special guests.</p> </div> </div> </div> </div> <p><strong>TICKETS</strong></p> <div class='style__notes___25v7J'> <div class='main-title'> <div class='TitleBlock__TitleMetaDataContainer-sc-1nlhx7j-2 hWHMKr'> <ul> <li><strong> Adults $50.00</strong></li> <li><strong>Youth: $20.00</strong></li> </ul> <p><em><span class='tm14'>HST additional</span></em></p> <ul> <li><em>Doors open 45 minutes before showtime.</em></li> <li><em>King’s Theatre is committed to accessibility. If price is a barrier to attending, please request a ‘Bursary Ticket’ at the Box Office.</em></li> <li><em>Tickets are not refundable for cash, but can be exchanged for credit with a minimum of 48 hours notice. Credits are valid for 12 months.</em></li> <li><em>All persons require a ticket; we do not allow babes in arms. Children under 12 must be accompanied by a guardian.</em></li> <li><em>Outside food and beverages may not be brought into the theatre.</em></li> <li><em>For more information about Theatre policies, click <a href='https://www.kingstheatre.ca/about/ticket-info/'>here.</a></em></li> </ul> </div> </div> </div> <p><iframe title='Christmas Day on Planet Earth - Lennie Gallant with Black Umfolosi' width='1080' height='608' src='https://www.youtube.com/embed/R5c7UOBhAKs?feature=oembed'  allow='accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share' referrerpolicy='strict-origin-when-cross-origin' allowfullscreen></iframe></p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> "
      }
