  {
    "@id": "https://kingstheatre.ca/events/event_242792_0",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Event"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.kingstheatre.ca/new-events/tara-mclean-the-bayfield-string-quartet/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.kingstheatre.ca/kingweb/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/TMac12-JenSquires.jpeg"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://kingstheatre.ca/events/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "TARA MACLEAN &amp; the Bayfield String Quartet"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<div dir='ltr'> <div dir='ltr'> <div dir='ltr'> <div dir='ltr'> <p><strong>On This Winter’s Night</strong></p> <p>A cozy and elegant evening of glistening winter music and storytelling with one of Canada’s foremost award-winning vocalists and best selling author, Tara MacLean. Joined by the Bayfield String Quartet, Tara will share a luminous blend of classic, contemporary, and original songs, curating an unforgettable night. Through song and story, On This Winter’s Night will wrap the audience in the magic of the season — weaving warmth, wonder, and holiday spirit into every heart.</p> </div> </div> </div> </div> <p><strong>TICKETS</strong></p> <div class='style__notes___25v7J'> <div class='main-title'> <div class='TitleBlock__TitleMetaDataContainer-sc-1nlhx7j-2 hWHMKr'> <ul> <li><strong> Adults $40.00</strong></li> <li><strong>Youth: $10.00</strong></li> </ul> <p><em><span class='tm14'>HST additional</span></em></p> </div> </div> </div> <p><strong>About the Tara MacLean:</strong></p> <p class='preFade fadeIn'>Canadian singer/songwriter Tara MacLean has been an internationally renowned and award winning recording and touring artist for over 25 years. She released her first album with the Nettwerk Music Group in 1996 and Sony Music Publishing Canada. Since then has been signed with Capitol Records, and EMI Canada with her JUNO nominated band <a href='https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shaye' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>Shaye</a>. She has written and recorded seven solo albums and two with Shaye.</p> <p class='preFade fadeIn'>Tara was awarded the Senate of Canada Medal for her activist work in her community. She finished a run of three summer seasons with her hit theater show that she wrote, produced, and directed called, “Atlantic Blue-The Stories of Atlantic Canada’s Iconic Songwriters” in Charlottetown. The summer of 2019 saw Atlantic Blue produced and directed by the world famous Charlottetown Festival playing three nights a week to sold out crowds.</p> <p><strong>About the Bayfield String Quartet:</strong></p> <p>The Bayfield String Quartet, known for their vibrant and engaging performances, is a dynamic ensemble that brings a fresh perspective to the string quartet tradition. Comprising four exceptional musicians—Karen Graves (violin), Kinley Dowling (violin), Jeffrey Bazett-Jones (viola), and Natalie Williams Calhoun (cello)—the quartet has quickly established itself in Charlottetown as one of the most compelling ensembles on the local chamber music scene. Each member of the Bayfield String Quartet brings a wealth of experience and individual artistry to the group. Together, they create a harmonious blend of voices that captivates audiences with its depth, clarity, and emotional power.</p> <p>Formed in 2024, the Bayfield String Quartet has been busy performing for the Candlelight concert series, sharing intimate house concerts and creating new shows to present on Prince Edward Island and beyond. Their performances are marked by their attention to detail, commitment to innovation, and the palpable chemistry between the musicians.</p> <p><iframe title='Tara MacLean - Sparrow (Official Video)' width='1080' height='608' src='https://www.youtube.com/embed/5W3tT8b5Wkc?feature=oembed'  allow='accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share' referrerpolicy='strict-origin-when-cross-origin' allowfullscreen></iframe></p> <p>&#8212;&#8212;&#8212;&#8212;&#8212;&#8212;&#8212;&#8212;-</p> <div class='style__notes___25v7J'> <div class='main-title'> <div class='TitleBlock__TitleMetaDataContainer-sc-1nlhx7j-2 hWHMKr'> <ul> <li><em>Doors open 45 minutes before showtime.</em></li> <li><em>King’s Theatre is committed to accessibility. If price is a barrier to attending, please request a ‘Bursary Ticket’ at the Box Office.</em></li> <li><em>Tickets are not refundable for cash, but can be exchanged for credit with a minimum of 48 hours notice. Credits are valid for 12 months.</em></li> <li><em>All persons require a ticket; we do not allow babes in arms. Children under 12 must be accompanied by a guardian.</em></li> <li><em>Outside food and beverages may not be brought into the theatre.</em></li> <li><em>For more information about Theatre policies, click <a href='https://www.kingstheatre.ca/about/ticket-info/'>here.</a></em></li> </ul> </div> </div> </div> <div></div> "
      }
    ],
