        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<p><strong>Presented by The Annapolis District Drama Group<br /> </strong><strong>Directed by Simon Bonnington and Dany Rousseau</strong></p> <p>Dany and Simon are delighted to bring to King&#8217;s Theatre stage &#8216;The Phoenix Showcase&#8217;, harnessing the boundless talents and experience of the Cast and Crew of the erstwhile &#8220;The Underpants&#8221; in an exciting, hilarious, slick and seamless journey in drama, dance and song.</p> <p><em>And, boy, does ADDG have a SHOW for you!!</em></p> <p>The audience will be whisked through a half-dozen short plays, ranging in performance length from 3 to 12 mins, which are carefully intertwined with hilarious Ensemble and Solo songs, deft and dazzling dance routines, and a brief monologue or two.</p> <p>From rum-smuggling to witch trials, old rumours to new homes, the monotony of work-life balance, and the travails of wannabe faded lights, hat and cane razzmatazz from Broadway, broken aspirations of misguided auditionees&#8230; and a horse&#8217;s head cane.</p> <p>Act 1 ~50 mins, Act 2 ~40 mins</p> <p class='gmail-western'><b>&#8216;Work-life Balance&#8217; – by Dany Rousseau</b></p> <p class='gmail-western'>Can frazzled bureaucrat Mr S achieve true happiness? Not if his well-intentioned secretary Joanne has anything to do about it. Is his frustration deliberately contrived? There&#8217;s a helluva chance it is!</p> <p class='gmail-western'><b>&#8216;Sight Unseen&#8217; – by Wayne Currie</b></p> <p class='gmail-western'>Come From Away newcomers find that small town living takes some getting used to, in a community where who you know might count for something. Or not! And is that a coyote? Or just the local friendly&#8230; bulldog?</p> <p class='gmail-western'><b>&#8216;A Second Opinion&#8217; – by Dany Rousseau</b></p> <p class='gmail-western'>Sassy bubble-gum chewing Anne faces down Salem&#8217;s Witchfinder; can her wit and back-chat force his hand, or like a moth will she flutter too close to the flames. Perhaps the staying hand of outside help might intervene?</p> <p class='gmail-western'><b>&#8216;A Rum Line To Nowhere&#8217; – by Simon Bonnington</b></p> <p class='gmail-western'>Down at Dory&#8217;s Dive Bar, where the whiff of seaweed, rum and gunpowder creates a heady haze for chisel-jawed wise-cracker Jack Raymond, as he seeks to solve Tommy&#8217;s murder, and unravel the smuggler&#8217;s secrets.</p> <p class='gmail-western'><b>&#8216;Much Ado About Method&#8217; – by Simon Bonnington</b></p> <p class='gmail-western'>The fraught Play Director has just about had enough. Faded light Julian cannot accept his shortcomings, the props are missing, the costumes don&#8217;t fit&#8230; and the Theatre itself has something to say about it!</p> <p class='gmail-western'><b>&#8216;Just Friends&#8217; – by Simon Bonnington</b></p> <p class='gmail-western'>That&#8217;s all we are! Honestly! But why let the truth get in the way of a good rumour? Especially when concerned neighbours and family attempt to set matters straight. Sorry, did we say concerned? Maybe we just meant nosy.</p> <p class='gmail-western'><b>Cast &amp; Crew:</b> (in Order of Appearance)</p> <ul> <li class='gmail-western'>Phil Milo</li> <li class='gmail-western'>Simon Bonnington</li> <li class='gmail-western'>Dany Rousseau</li> <li class='gmail-western'>Pierce Ivan</li> <li class='gmail-western'>Shaeralee McCutcheon</li> <li class='gmail-western'>Diane Sokoloski</li> <li class='gmail-western'>Christine Connolly</li> <li class='gmail-western'>Ryan Terry</li> <li class='gmail-western'>AC Silver</li> <li class='gmail-western'>Ryan Hebert</li> <li class='gmail-western'>Miles Leahy</li> </ul> <p class='gmail-western'><b>Backstage:</b></p> <ul> <li class='gmail-western'>Mackenzie Shields</li> <li class='gmail-western'>Connor McCutcheon</li> <li class='gmail-western'>Anna Emery</li> <li class='gmail-western'>Dawn Scott</li> </ul> <p><strong>TICKETS:</strong></p> <ul> <li><strong>Adults: $22</strong></li> <li><strong>Youth: $10 (Under 18)</strong></li> </ul> <p>&nbsp;</p> <ul> <li> <div class='style__notes___25v7J'> <div class='main-title'> <div class='TitleBlock__TitleMetaDataContainer-sc-1nlhx7j-2 hWHMKr'> <ul> <li><em>Doors open 45 minutes before showtime.</em></li> <li><em>King’s Theatre is committed to accessibility. If price is a barrier to attending, please request a ‘Bursary Ticket’ at the Box Office.</em></li> <li><em>Tickets are not refundable for cash, but can be exchanged for credit with a minimum of 48 hours notice. Credits are valid for 12 months.</em></li> <li><em>All persons require a ticket; we do not allow babes in arms. Children under 12 must be accompanied by a guardian.</em></li> <li><em>Outside food and beverages may not be brought into the theatre.</em></li> <li><em>For more information about Theatre policies, click <a href='https://www.kingstheatre.ca/about/ticket-info/'>here.</a></em></li> </ul> </div> </div> </div> </li> </ul> "
      }
    ],
